      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd CPU-only canonical KV mapping byte tests for TP=2, PCP=2, as requested by @Etelis in #61886.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Cover split/packed NHD and HND layouts with interleave sizes 1 and 2 (8 cases).\n- Verify canonical reconstruction and per-rank readback against independent reference bytes.\n- Preserve existing portability restrictions without production changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- **35 passed** — full canonical mapping test suite.\n- **8/8 mutation tests** detected deliberately incorrect PCP token placement while tiling still passed.\n- All applicable pre-commit hooks passed.\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu .venv/bin/python -m pytest -v \\\n  tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/offloading_connector/test_canonical_mapping.py\n```\n\n## Details\n\nExisting tiling and round-trip tests can miss symmetric byte-placement errors. These tests use independently generated K/V, token, and head reference data to verify exact placement.\n\nReuses existing helpers. CPU-only, 57 lines added to one test file. No GPU execution or production changes.\n\nRelated PRs #62160 and #62162 address separate functionality.\n\n**AI assistance:** Codex assisted with implementation and validation. I reviewed the changes and verified the tests.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill.\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Reuses existing functionality without production changes.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Meaningful tests with passing validation.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** All applicable checks passed.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes scope, evidence, and relevant issues.\n\n</details>\n\n",
